      - or unlocked via pages from quest progression, similar to the journal currently
      - the lore pages about the BL could also be added here, and then remove the Journal mod

How To Unlock Thaumcraft:
  ☐ once the player has made syrmorite, trigger an invasion the next day (or few ingame hours)
  ☐ after the invasion (a dark druid), the player finds an entry in their journal about finding the Druid Altar to craft Salis Mundus (also this needs to trigger the thaumcraft journal book thing)
  ☐ killing a druid at the altar should also count as having killed the invasion druid
  ☐ the book / note that drops should just tell the player about the salis mundus recipe, but they should be able to craft it without the book as well 


Cheeeeeese:
  ☣ Churnrot (Cheddar equivalent)
“The Crumbly Blight”

Aged in decaying Betweenstone sarcophagi, packed with mulch and blood-leaf pulp.
Its rind hardens to a bark-like crust, while the inside breaks apart like moist clay.
Effect: Grants mild resistance to rot but may attract Leeches if consumed at dusk.
Quote: “It don’t melt—it peels.”

🦠 Sporemelt (Asiago equivalent)
“The Singing Curd”

Curdled with Sludge Worm enzymes and wrapped in fungal gills from Weeping Caps.
As it matures, faint humming emerges from inside the rind—often mistaken for swamp spirits.
Effect: Allows the eater to hear whispers of nearby Wisps for 3 minutes.
Quote: “Plug your ears, or your thoughts’ll turn to mud.”

🪨 Graveflake (Parmesan equivalent)
“Shards of the Dead Mire”

Made brittle by mixing in powdered Sulfur Crystal and hanging it above Rotting Bogs to dry.
Commonly shaved onto Gloomtatoes or Bloodsnail stew.
Effect: Undead mobs may ignore the eater temporarily.
Quote: “Sharp enough to kill taste—and most pests.”

🌿 Fenbliss (Monterey equivalent)
“The Gentle Mold”

Soft, herbal cheese soaked in Sundew nectar and aged inside hollow Weedwood trunks.
Consumed by Swamp Hags during trances; considered a delicacy by Tree Spirits.
Effect: Temporarily calms fear effects and causes hallucinations of floating moths.
Quote: “It sighs when you bite it.”

🕸 Tanglecurd (Provolone equivalent)
“The Web-Aged Wheel”

Bound in Dry Bark and hung in Giant Webbed Grass clusters. The spiders ignore it—supposedly out of respect.
Has a strong, smoky profile and chewy texture.
Effect: Briefly increases jump height and allows walking through cobwebs unhindered.
Quote: “Stickier than guilt.”

💡 Glowcurd (Gouda equivalent)
“The Lantern Milk”

Infused with light-emitting Swamp Reeds and Bog Bulb essence. Glows faint green.
Must be stored in Shadow Chests or it draws the attention of Mirebats.
Effect: Emits light when held; repels Wights in a small radius.
Quote: “Only food that doubles as a torch.”



