Triumph/Patchouli notes:
  - quests are advancements
  - use triumph to setup advancements
  - use triumph to define the actual reward (addRewardItem)
  - use patchouli to display what you need to get and what you'll get in return (it's just visual)
  - "/reload" to reload triumph configs



Useful tips for testers:
  - biomes are set to large, craft a nature's compass or map to find other biomes
  - to make string, get silkworm eggs by breaking any leaves, hatch em, and once hatched, right click weedwood stick bundle
  - to get new thaumcraft research, drink teas (each tea is for a different research category). Also requires thaumonomicon and quill in inventory
  - there is a hidden pacifist challenge in which you are not allowed to kill passive animals (except for fish). Doing so gives some bonuses, like a shorter cooldown on runic shears
  


Testers:
  Fariardo3 (from mischief twitch chat)
  jjallie



Story:
  - your world is slowly dying (spreading corruption) and you are tasked to explore dimensions to find a new home
  - the one you are meant to explore is a dimension between dimensions, therefore people are theorizing that it will be immune to the corruption that is spreading from dimension to dimension
    - the corruption could be the taint/emptieness? Meaning it can still occur, but is slowed down due to the dimensions own decay?
  - player enters dimension to find out if it's stable, and to re-connect with their people afterwards
  - player can find notes of "the first visitor" (who will eventually turn out to be the prime wight, or be taken over by the prime wight (later one makes more sense?))
  - slowly learn that even though the taint can reach the dimension, the decay is slowing it down
    - the decay is not a bad thing, it's life in its own form, and is what keeps the world alive, in a strange way
  - before the player builds the last item to get back home, the note from the first visitor will mention that this is as far as they made it (either died or taken over by prime wight)
  - when player makes it back, dimension is totally destroyed
  - there is a note form the person giving you your task, saying that they had to move on to another place for now (only saved a few people) and task the player to prepare in case more survivors arrive in the betweenlands
  - player can go back to betweenlands and the pack ends here (until prime wight update?)
  - last item to teleport back home is the fabricated wayfinder
  Lore Entries:
    - initial task from the elder
      - tell player to go into this dimension that lies "between" two other dimensions
    - first note from the visitor
    - maybe replace the BL notes with lore pages?
    - taint
      - what it is (discover its the corruption)
      - discover decay slows it down
      - discover it's origin point (the emptieness)
    - last note from the visitor
      - taken over by the prime wight
    - last note from the elder
      - moved on, tel player to stay behind to help survivors in case they show up




